INFO:__main__:Prompt Metadata:
INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:{    "action": "I find myself in a strange, unfamiliar place surrounded by rolling hills, patches of trees, and a small stream. I can feel a gentle breeze on my skin, and the air feels cool but not uncomfortable. My body feels a bit tired and hungry, with a slight dryness in my throat, and I notice a mild ache in my limbs, though nothing too severe. I don’t understand much about my surroundings or myself yet, but I can sense that I need to take care of my immediate needs to feel better.\n\nLooking around, I see the stream nearby with clear water. Since my throat feels dry, I decide to walk toward the stream to drink some water. I move slowly, feeling the uneven ground under my feet and being cautious not to slip or hurt myself further. When I reach the stream, I kneel down and cup my hands to scoop up some water, drinking it to ease my thirst. The water feels cold and refreshing, and I take a moment to splash some on my face, which helps wake me up a little.\n\nI also notice my stomach grumbling, and I see some plants around that look different from the grass—maybe they’re safe to eat. I don’t know much about them, though, so I hesitate. I decide to pick a small amount of one type of plant, just to test it later if I get hungrier. For now, I focus on finding a safe spot to rest since my body feels low on energy. I see some natural overhangs in the hills and clusters of trees that might offer protection from the breeze or any unexpected changes in the air. I choose to move toward a nearby overhang that looks dry and shielded, hoping to sit there and observe my surroundings more while I regain some strength.\n\nMy reasoning for these actions is simple: I feel thirsty, hungry, and tired, and I’m acting on those feelings to make myself more comfortable. I don’t know what dangers might be out here, so I’m moving carefully and prioritizing safety by finding a sheltered spot. I’m also curious about the plants and the small animals I see, but I’m unsure how to approach them yet, so I’m holding off on taking risks until I understand more.\n\nWhat I’ve learned from this experience:\n1. Drinking water from a stream can ease thirst and feels refreshing.\n2. My body feels better when I address basic needs like thirst.\n3. Natural overhangs and tree clusters can provide shelter and a sense of safety.\n4. I should be cautious about eating unknown plants or approaching wildlife until I learn more about them.\n5. Moving slowly and observing my surroundings helps me avoid potential harm."}
