INFO:__main__:Prompt Metadata:
INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:{    "action": "Given the current conditions of mid-morning warmth, clear skies, and my status of moderate hunger (5) and low energy (4), I will focus on foraging for food in the woodland area near the rolling hills to address my hunger and hopefully boost my energy. My overall health (6) and minor injuries (2) suggest I can handle light activity, but I must conserve energy and avoid overexertion, as learned from previous experiences. I’ll head to the woodland foraging spot, which I remember as having edible-looking plants and berries, though partially depleted. I will cautiously select a small amount of plants or berries I’ve previously tested or that look similar to those I’ve found safe, chewing slowly and waiting to observe any adverse reactions, as I’ve learned caution is critical with unknown food sources. I’ll also keep an eye on the cautious small rodents in the area, using my wildlife observation skill to move slowly and avoid startling them, in case they could be a future food source, though I won’t attempt to catch them now due to my limited energy. While foraging, I’ll stay aware of my surroundings for any changes in wildlife behavior, especially since nocturnal predators like foxes linger in the periphery, even if the danger level is low. After foraging, I plan to return to my shelter under the natural overhang to rest and consume what I’ve gathered, ensuring I’m in a safe spot to recover energy. I’m choosing this action because addressing hunger is a priority for maintaining my strength, and the mid-morning light offers a safer time to explore compared to evening or night, as visibility is better and predators are less active. Additionally, staying near known locations like the stream and shelter reduces the risk of getting lost or encountering unexpected dangers. My past experiences have taught me the importance of small, cautious steps with food and the value of conserving energy, which guides my decision to limit this activity to foraging and returning to rest rather than pushing further exploration."}
