            "danger_level": "Low (high luck factor and mid-afternoon light minimize threats; cautious wildlife poses little immediate risk; rest at shelter reduces fatigue risk)",
            "notes_for_future": {
                "wildlife_alert": "Fish in the stream have become even more alert due to the agent's recent presence and observation near the stream, making fishing attempts increasingly difficult without tools or preparation. Small rodents and herbivores remain extremely cautious due to prior activity, continuing to be hard to approach or catch. Nocturnal predators like foxes maintain mild curiosity and may become more active as evening approaches; high luck factor prevents immediate confrontation for now.",
                "resource_change": "No change in food availability as the agent chose to rest and not forage; edible plants remain extremely scarce in immediate and nearby areas, moderate in deeper woodland. Water availability unchanged, with successful collection from the stream ensuring hydration needs are met for now. Shelter remains stable and occupied, providing a secure resting spot.",
                "environmental_shift": "Time progresses to mid-afternoon; temperature rises slightly with continued sunlight, maintaining warm and comfortable conditions. Clear skies and gentle breeze persist, supported by high luck factor, ensuring stable weather for the immediate future. Visibility remains good but will start to decrease as evening approaches, potentially affecting resource gathering or threat detection in the coming hours."
            }
        },
        "AIAH_Alive": "Alive",
