INFO:__main__:Prompt Metadata:
INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:{    "action": "Given the early morning light, clear skies, and low to moderate danger level, I will focus on addressing my immediate needs while conserving my limited energy. My hunger level is high at 7, and my energy is low at 5, which, combined with an overall health of 5 and minor injuries, means I must prioritize actions that minimize exertion while maximizing benefit. Thirst is manageable at 3, thanks to the accessible stream water, so hydration is not an urgent concern, but I will still collect water to maintain my status. The critical depletion of edible plants in immediate and nearby areas, as well as the very low availability in deeper woodland, pushes me to explore slightly further into the deeper woodland for any remaining food sources, relying on my refined skills in cautious foraging and exploration for resources. I will move slowly and deliberately to avoid overexertion, focusing only on gathering any edible plants I can find with minimal energy expenditure. I will also collect water from the stream on my way back to ensure hydration needs are met. Hunting rodents or fish is not feasible given their extreme caution and my lack of tools or energy to pursue them, so I will continue passive wildlife observation if possible, to build knowledge for future attempts when my condition improves. My shelter under the natural overhang is stable and secure, so I plan to return there after foraging to rest and avoid any potential threats, especially since nocturnal predators like foxes are retreating with the dawn. My decision to forage now is based on the safer conditions of early morning light, as learned from past experiences, and the high luck factor of 10 that has consistently mitigated risks. I am aware of the sustainability concerns from continued foraging, as reflected in my diary, and feel a sense of guilt for depleting resources further, but addressing hunger is critical for my survival at this moment. I will limit my foraging to only what I need for the day to reduce impact. Emotionally, I feel a mix of relief for the safer daylight conditions and anxiety about my physical state and the scarcity of resources, but I am determined to push forward cautiously. The lessons from my diary about timing actions during safer hours and conserving energy guide this choice, as does the need to balance immediate survival with long-term resource management."}
